      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you think about adding a command which returns a port and an address? I think it has a few advantages over a virtual port \u0026 address solution.\n\n1. Such a command can be used for other purposes. For example, a developer can see what other chips are on the bus. \n\n2. i2cprotect takes a port #. It doesn\u0027t use i2c passthrough.\n\n3. We can keep i2c_command_passthru simple (which is already complicated). Translation doesn\u0027t have to be repeated. If translation fails, we can know it explicitly (instead of receiving EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 751,
